    "body": "## Movement Electronic Music Festival\n\nLaunched in 2000 as the free Detroit Electronic Music Festival, curated by Carl Craig and Carol Marvin's Pop Culture Media at Hart Plaza. Derrick May took over organizing in 2003 and renamed it Movement; it later became the ticketed Memorial Day weekend fixture.\n\nHeld every Memorial Day weekend at Hart Plaza, Movement is the spiritual home of American electronic music, pairing [Detroit house](/topic/detroit-house) and techno with house from around the world. The full lineup history is mapped in this database's directory.\n\n### Detroit originators & house artists associated with Movement\n\n- [Carl Craig](/artist/carl-craig)\n- **Derrick May**\n- [Kevin Saunderson](/artist/kevin-saunderson)\n- [Stacey Pullen](/artist/stacey-pullen)\n- [Moodymann](/artist/moodymann)\n- [Theo Parrish](/artist/theo-parrish)\n- **Richie Hawtin**\n\nSee also: the [festivals overview](/topic/house-music-festivals) and [Detroit house history](/topic/detroit-house)."
